{
  "dom_id": "step-q119796",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251721/assets/aa72f6ea8c52a1f141f8469c3f932937b8b957956dc478811910e77c83336a9c.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $p?$",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251721/assets/4d4d7faa0c0611c8ef891cda5fef3b75a61aa97e0879fac525f58f4ce263c937.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$, we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=2$ and $BH=5.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $p$ is $\\sqrt{29}.$ Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{1}{|\\,p\\,|}\\cdot p \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{29}}p.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
